                            {
                                "example_id": "c1808bef-7364-4f16-93a8-9e85e8fb04b1",
                                "sense_id": "00e4e785-8a77-3be7-8e6b-5a837eb18e29",
                                "text": "Einen solchen Diffeomorphismus H#58;W#92;rightarrowW' wollen wir, seiner anschaulichen Bedeutung nach, auch einen Flachmacher für M um p nennen. In einer anderen Sprechweise heißt ein Flachmacher H#58;W#92;rightarrowW' eine äußere Karte für M um p#92;inM, im Unterschied nämlich zur zugehörigen inneren Karte H#124;M#92;cupW: […]",
                                "translation": "We want to additionally call such a diffeomorphism H:W→W', in accordance with its illustrative meaning, a flat maker for M around p. In another mode of speaking, a flat maker H:W→W' is also named an outer chart for M around p∈M, in contrast namely to the corresponding inner chart H|M∪W: […]",
                                "english": "We want to additionally call such a diffeomorphism H:W→W', in accordance with its illustrative meaning, a flat maker for M around p. In another mode of speaking, a flat maker H:W→W' is also named an outer chart for M around p∈M, in contrast namely to the corresponding inner chart H|M∪W: […]"
